---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Services — Signal Advisory · Independent Telecom & Cloud Advisor"
  description="Carrier sourcing, technology advisory, and managed services for IT teams renegotiating telecom, cloud, and UCaaS contracts. Buyer-side. Independent."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pb-20 pt-20 md:px-10 md:pt-28">
    <p class="mb-5 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone">Services</p>
    <h1 class="display text-5xl font-light leading-[0.95] md:text-6xl">
      We work for the buyer.<br />
      <em class="text-signal not-italic font-medium">Not the carrier.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
      Three disciplines. One trusted advisor. Hourly or retained — no carrier commissions
      tied to recommendations, no quota driving our advice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 01: Carrier sourcing -->
  <section id="carrier-sourcing" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">01</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Carrier sourcing</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            SD-WAN · UCaaS · DIA · SASE · MPLS · Mobility
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            One advisor, every carrier evaluated. Most organizations have 4–6 carrier relationships
            split across internet, voice, mobile, and SD-WAN, with separate account teams and renewal
            cycles at each. We assess the entire market on your behalf — Spectrum, AT&T, Verizon, Lumen,
            Comcast Business, Cox, Frontier, and dozens more — negotiate the terms, and stay on the
            account for the life of the relationship.
          </p>
          <p>
            What's different about working with us versus a traditional master-agent agent: we don't
            carry a quota for any single provider. Our recommendations aren't downstream of which
            carrier pays a higher residual. They're downstream of which carrier actually serves your
            footprint, term flexibility, and operational requirements best.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Engagements typically address:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Upcoming renewals on existing carrier contracts (start 6–9 months out for maximum leverage)</li>
            <li>New site builds, M&A integration, location consolidation</li>
            <li>MPLS-to-SD-WAN transitions and SASE evaluations</li>
            <li>PBX-to-UCaaS migrations (RingCentral, 8x8, Zoom Phone, Cisco Webex Calling)</li>
            <li>Mobile fleet renegotiation and TEM (telecom expense management) setup</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02: Technology advisory -->
  <section id="technology-advisory" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink/[0.03] py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">02</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Technology advisory</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            Vendor selection · Contract review · Architecture
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Independent counsel on what to buy, who to buy it from, and how to structure the
            agreement. Hourly or retained — we provide expertise your team needs without the bias
            of a vendor relationship and without adding headcount.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Common engagements:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Carrier contract review.</strong> Send us your last 3 months of invoices and current MSA. We come back with a marked-up version flagging renegotiable line items, term traps, and SLA gaps. Most reviews surface 8–15% of annual spend in addressable savings.</li>
            <li><strong>RFP support.</strong> We write the requirements doc, run the bid, score the responses, and present a recommendation. Saves IT teams 80–120 hours per RFP.</li>
            <li><strong>Architecture planning.</strong> SD-WAN vs SASE vs hybrid, single-carrier vs diversified, on-prem vs cloud UC. We bring carrier-agnostic perspective on what your specific footprint actually needs.</li>
            <li><strong>Implementation oversight.</strong> Carrier projects ship late. We sit between your team and the carrier project manager to keep things accountable.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If we cannot find cost reduction across your IT spend in an initial review, we pay you for
            the hour you spent with us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03: Managed services -->
  <section id="managed-services" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">03</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Managed services</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            Operations · Escalations · Invoice auditing
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Once the contract is signed, the operational headache begins. Carrier project managers
            change every six months. Tickets sit in queues. Billing errors compound. We absorb that
            work so your IT team doesn't have to.
          </p>
          <p><strong>What we manage:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Implementation oversight — coordinating the carrier's project team, the LEC, and your network team through delivery</li>
            <li>Tier-2 escalations on tickets that get stuck</li>
            <li>Monthly invoice auditing — billing errors run 3–6% of telecom invoices on average</li>
            <li>Carrier portal administration (account access, MACDs, ticket logging)</li>
            <li>Quarterly business reviews — vendor scorecards, spend trending, renewal forecasting</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Retained on a monthly basis. Typically pays for itself in invoice errors caught + soft-cost
            offload from your team.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <section id="pricing" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <p class="mb-4 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone">Pricing</p>
      <h2 class="display mb-6 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-normal leading-tight md:text-5xl">
        Published rates. No retainers we can't justify.
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-16 max-w-3xl text-ink/70 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        We charge clients directly, not carriers. That means our recommendations on which provider, term, or architecture aren't downstream of who'd pay us a bigger commission. Three engagement structures depending on what you need.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="border border-ink/15 p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">HOURLY</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">$250<span class="text-xl text-ink/60">/hr</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Discrete questions, single-vendor review, second-opinion calls.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Ad-hoc consultation</li>
            <li>· No minimum engagement</li>
            <li>· Billed monthly against time used</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border-2 border-signal p-8 relative">
          <p class="absolute -top-3 left-8 bg-signal text-paper text-xs uppercase tracking-wider px-3 py-1">Most common</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">CONTRACT REVIEW</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">$2,500<span class="text-xl text-ink/60"> flat</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">One renewal, one decision, one defined deliverable.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Invoice and contract audit</li>
            <li>· Marked-up MSA with renegotiation targets</li>
            <li>· Competitive baseline (3 carrier quotes)</li>
            <li>· 1-hour strategy session before you sign</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-ink/15 p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">RETAINED</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">From $3k<span class="text-xl text-ink/60">/mo</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Ongoing vendor management, multi-site oversight, quarterly reviews.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Monthly invoice auditing</li>
            <li>· Renewal calendar management</li>
            <li>· Tier-2 ticket escalations</li>
            <li>· Quarterly business reviews</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12 bg-ink/[0.03] -mx-6 px-6 py-10 md:-mx-10 md:px-10">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-signal mb-3">THE GUARANTEE</p>
          <h3 class="display text-2xl font-medium text-ink mb-4">
            If we can't find at least $250/month in savings, the review is free.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
            We start every engagement with a free 30-minute scoping call and an invoice review. If
            we don't see a clear path to at least $250 in monthly recurring savings on your
            existing IT spend, you don't pay for the time we spent. No invoice, no follow-up. We
            offer this because in 9 out of 10 mid-market reviews we run, the savings clear the
            threshold inside the first 20 minutes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink py-24 text-paper">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center md:px-10">
      <h2 class="display mb-6 text-4xl font-normal leading-tight md:text-5xl">
        Ready to look at the numbers?
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-10 text-lg text-paper/60 leading-relaxed">
        Send us your last carrier invoice. We'll mark up what we'd renegotiate, no obligation.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/audit"
          class="inline-block rounded-sm bg-signal px-8 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-paper hover:bg-paper hover:text-ink transition-colors"
        >
          Free invoice audit
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://calendly.com/signaladvise-info/30min"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block rounded-sm border border-paper/30 px-8 py-4 text-sm font-medium hover:border-paper transition-colors"
        >
          Schedule a 30-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
